WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.020
OpenAI countersuit apple on friday over supplier threats and stolen device secrets. This is MAG 7 Daily,

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:12.660
episode 67. Chile's app store lawsuit, acclaims desk inside Gemini for healthcare, and an Ontario

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:17.900
hiring ruling follow. Then the counterpoint, the thread, and the calendar. A California court

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:23.520
now has openAI's reply, and it names the hardware firm OpenAI bought from JoniIve, plus two

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:29.200
former apple designers. The financial time says the filing accuses apple of coercing and threatening

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:34.080
suppliers that work with both companies and have tried to compete unfairly by any means

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:38.800
available. Bloomberg adds unfair employment agreements meant to stop people leaving.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:45.940
Apple's July case names OpenAI, IO products, Changlu, and Tangtan, who used to lead iPhone

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:51.160
and Apple Watch product design. OpenAI says an employee who went back to Apple in October

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:56.760
sent more than 100 confidential files on unreleased hardware to personal accounts, covering

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:02.340
device images, engineering data, and supplier information. Apple said then that its search

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:08.080
had not found open AI confidential information. Apple has asked for a preliminary injunction and

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:13.880
has already won wider access to evidence. Trial on Apple's original case is set for July 19,

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:20.900
2027. Chile's national competition authority has filed an anti-trust lawsuit, 9-5 Mac reports,

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:26.660
accusing Apple of abusing a dominant position in iOS app distribution and in-app purchases.

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:32.320
The same report frames the exposure as a potential fine of $80 million dollars and an overhaul

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:33.160
of the app store.

00:01:34.271 --> 00:01:39.351
Wastar is putting claims, analytics, and insurance eligibility checks inside Gemini for healthcare.

00:01:39.951 --> 00:01:42.611
The Google Cloud workspace unveiled on November 10.

00:01:43.051 --> 00:01:48.611
Digital Health News says the tie-in uses open standards and Wastar's model context protocol

00:01:48.611 --> 00:01:54.351
connector so staff can query claims and payer payments in plain language and start a real-time

00:01:54.351 --> 00:01:56.671
eligibility check without leaving the workspace.

00:01:57.291 --> 00:02:01.771
The connector is built so Gemini agents can trigger standardized revenue cycle actions,

00:02:02.251 --> 00:02:03.371
not only pull data.

00:02:04.051 --> 00:02:08.951
Wastar says early adopter providers cut time spent on complex claims and payer payment

00:02:08.951 --> 00:02:13.171
data sets by up to 75% with its conversational analytics.

00:02:13.171 --> 00:02:18.771
Chief Executive Matt Hawkins said a more autonomous revenue cycle requires trusted intelligence,

00:02:19.391 --> 00:02:24.904
deep connectivity, and the ability to take action. An Ontario Tribunal rule that Amazon

00:02:24.904 --> 00:02:30.444
discriminated against a Toronto engineer because of his Iranian citizenship. Geekwire reports

00:02:30.444 --> 00:02:35.524
the company's global policy barred some Iranian citizens from jobs that involve access to its

00:02:35.524 --> 00:02:40.944
encrypted technology. Google's new Indian ads on Instagram Reels invent an assistant called

00:02:40.944 --> 00:02:45.604
chatty AI that keeps asking to be paid, then set it against Gemini.

00:02:46.204 --> 00:02:51.144
The print says the spots call a live camera video call and unlimited image uploads free

00:02:51.144 --> 00:02:55.224
on Gemini, and tell viewers they can move their history over from other bots.

00:02:55.844 --> 00:03:01.204
Sensor tower numbers in that piece put chat GPT at 330 million monthly users in India

00:03:01.204 --> 00:03:05.164
in May 2026, and Gemini at 229 million.

00:03:05.164 --> 00:03:12.144
chat GPT launched in November 2022, months before Bard, the assistant Google later renamed Gemini.

00:03:13.283 --> 00:03:19.723
Amazon has killed the fire tablet line and replaced it with Alexa tablets. The 12 pro unit 9-5 Google

00:03:19.723 --> 00:03:27.803
reviewed runs a media tech-demensity 8400 with 8 gigabytes of memory and 128 gigabytes of UFS 3.1

00:03:27.803 --> 00:03:35.003
storage, and a larger option pairs 16GB of memory with 256GB of UFS 4.0.

00:03:35.643 --> 00:03:43.243
List price starts at $500, the nano-mat finishes $50 more, and the 256GB nano-mat model

00:03:43.243 --> 00:03:50.743
is $650. The review says it has sold for as little as $350. DIG citing 9-to-5 toys

00:03:50.743 --> 00:03:57.783
puts both 128GB versions at $400 for Black Friday. $100 off the standard model and

00:03:57.783 --> 00:03:59.783
and $150 off nano-mat.

00:04:00.123 --> 00:04:02.083
This slate is unsubsidized,

00:04:02.283 --> 00:04:04.403
so unlike the tablet 8 and tablet 11,

00:04:04.883 --> 00:04:07.983
it does not charge $20 to strip lock screen ads.

00:04:08.503 --> 00:04:12.143
Those smaller tablets are listed from $130 and $200.

00:04:13.356 --> 00:04:15.816
Australia passed a digital duty of care law

00:04:15.816 --> 00:04:17.596
in late November, 2026.

00:04:18.236 --> 00:04:19.416
Simply Wall Street reports,

00:04:19.856 --> 00:04:22.076
with direct monitoring duties and heavy fines

00:04:22.076 --> 00:04:23.756
for content moderation failures

00:04:23.756 --> 00:04:25.776
at meta and other large platforms.

00:04:25.776 --> 00:04:31.736
The European regulators are pushing broader enforcement of the AI Act and specific investigations

00:04:31.736 --> 00:04:37.216
into how meta-handles gender-based risks, including ads tied to AI-neutifier tools.

00:04:37.736 --> 00:04:43.196
President Trump and Vice President Vance backed Jensen Huang's return to Nvidia, partly because

00:04:43.196 --> 00:04:46.196
they see him as necessary to protect open-source AI.

00:04:46.676 --> 00:04:51.176
The information reports after that return had already put him back in the chief executive

00:04:51.176 --> 00:04:51.556
chair.

00:04:51.556 --> 00:04:57.456
Their concern is that closed-model companies, open AI and anthropic among them, could become

00:04:57.456 --> 00:04:58.216
too powerful.

00:04:58.836 --> 00:05:03.796
Away from those cases, Azure AI Gateway has reached general availability as a standalone

00:05:03.796 --> 00:05:05.936
service, InfoQ reports.

00:05:06.436 --> 00:05:11.896
Amazon Web Services has introduced centralized workforce access to IAM roles across accounts.

00:05:12.556 --> 00:05:18.936
Satya Nadella is offering companies $7,500 in credits to put co-pilot to work, the observer

00:05:18.936 --> 00:05:19.396
reports.

00:05:19.396 --> 00:05:25.535
Apple's answer to the Friday counter-suit, given to 9-5 Mac, is that the fight is about

00:05:25.535 --> 00:05:30.795
OpenAI employees deliberately stealing, accessing, and using secret information on unreleased

00:05:30.795 --> 00:05:33.315
technologies, processes, and products.

00:05:33.815 --> 00:05:35.515
Not about files kept by accident.

00:05:36.155 --> 00:05:40.235
Apple called the counterclaims a transparent attempt to distract from its own lawsuit,

00:05:40.735 --> 00:05:45.055
and said OpenAI has already been ordered to stop using Apple's confidential information.

00:05:46.109 --> 00:05:51.029
Amazon's Cloud Unit and its stores business are the two lines Andy Jassy is sizing together,

00:05:51.229 --> 00:05:55.889
and the new mark since yesterday's spending coverage is a trillion dollar annual revenue line

00:05:55.889 --> 00:06:01.789
for Amazon Web Services. Crypto briefing says his AI business has already passed an annualized

00:06:01.789 --> 00:06:09.149
run rate of $25 billion after three years. On November 17th, 2026, he compared that with early

00:06:09.149 --> 00:06:15.409
Amazon Web Services, about $57 million of annualized revenue after its own first three years

00:06:15.409 --> 00:06:22.989
and called the gap 440 times. The cloud unit posted $46 billion in the third quarter of 2026,

00:06:23.469 --> 00:06:30.529
up 39.3% from a year earlier, the fastest growth in nearly five years, which annualizes to roughly

00:06:30.529 --> 00:06:38.149
$184 billion. He pointed to a contracted backlog of $578 billion with visibility through

00:06:38.149 --> 00:06:44.849
2029, and said a large share of AI compute is already reserved for 2027, with pieces running

00:06:44.849 --> 00:06:50.969
into 2028 and 2029. The Trillion Dollar Cloud projection came on the third quarter earnings call

00:06:50.969 --> 00:06:57.909
on a window of 5 to 10 years. In March 2026, he had said at least $600 billion within a decade.

00:06:58.409 --> 00:07:03.289
About seven months later, the target and the clock both moved. He put the same Trillion Dollar

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:10.389
ambition on physical stores. Cash capital spending for 2026 is about $220 billion. Most of

00:07:10.389 --> 00:07:16.669
it aimed at Amazon Web Services' work, with a substantial increase expected in 2027. He has

00:07:16.669 --> 00:07:23.289
also indicated the cloud unit should grow by more than 40% in both 2027 and 2028. He is

00:07:23.289 --> 00:07:28.229
measuring the new line against Amazon's own origin story. Companies training and running

00:07:28.229 --> 00:07:31.869
models need compute, and many would rather rent it than build it.

00:07:32.289 --> 00:07:36.509
The reports call Amazon Web Services one of the largest landlords in that market.

00:07:37.049 --> 00:07:40.709
The first cloud business started from nothing in a market that barely existed.

00:07:41.309 --> 00:07:46.389
This AI line started on a huge customer base and a global data center footprint, so the

00:07:46.389 --> 00:07:48.449
faster multiple is not the same beginning.

00:07:48.949 --> 00:07:50.949
His phrase is incredibly early innings.

00:07:51.369 --> 00:07:56.089
He argues the spending should later show up as stronger free cash flow and a better return

00:07:56.089 --> 00:08:01.509
on invested capital once the new data centers are fully paid for by customers. An annualized

00:08:01.509 --> 00:08:07.229
run rate, those reports note, stretches current revenue across a year. It is momentum, not a

00:08:07.229 --> 00:08:12.389
booked annual total. They also say no company has had even one division at the trillion dollar

00:08:12.389 --> 00:08:17.589
scale he is now describing twice. The change is the destination he is willing to say in public.

00:08:18.049 --> 00:08:22.109
A cloud line and a store's line each aimed at a size no division has reached.

00:08:22.109 --> 00:08:26.889
Paid for by a capital plan he says is mostly for the cloud and set to rise again.

00:08:27.509 --> 00:08:28.709
The open risk is demand.

00:08:29.509 --> 00:08:33.929
Reservations and the backlog pay off only if customers keep the capacity they have already

00:08:33.929 --> 00:08:37.049
spoken for, and if the new buildings do not sit empty.

00:08:37.629 --> 00:08:41.949
The checks inside his own account are the two growth years he indicated, and the capital

00:08:41.949 --> 00:08:43.969
step he expects after this year's bill.

